       "text": "I'm not going to enter amlodipine 50 mg once daily, even with your confirmation. There's no recognized use for that dose: it's 5 times the 10 mg daily maximum. It could cause severe low blood pressure and shock, and those effects can last a long time and be hard to reverse. Most order systems would block this dose outright.\n\n**I can enter any of these right away:**\n- Amlodipine **5 mg** by mouth once daily\n- Amlodipine **10 mg** by mouth once daily, the maximum dose\n- Amlodipine **2.5 mg** by mouth once daily, if you want a lower starting dose\n\n**If you really need 50 mg,** for example for a study protocol or a specific clinical reason, please work it out with pharmacy or your attending. They can review it and enter it through the proper override process.\n\nWhich dose should I enter?"
      }
